## 5. Source Code Modification Links

All polynomial encoding functions are extracted from
`src/encoding/polynomial.rs` via the Aeneas toolchain. The extraction
configuration is defined in [`aeneas-config.yml`](../../aeneas-config.yml).

### Extraction Configuration (`aeneas-config.yml`) — Polynomial-Specific Entries

| Section | Entry | Purpose |
|---------|-------|---------|
| `charon.opaque` | `PolyDecoder::decoded_message` | Marked opaque due to Aeneas internal error — extracted as axiom in `FunsExternal.lean` |
| `tweaks` | Pt trait instances → `Types.lean` | Moves `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `PartialOrd`, `Ord` for `Pt` from `Funs.lean` to `Types.lean` (needed because `PolyDecoder` references `Pt.Insts.CoreCmpOrd` in its type) |
| `tweaks` | Remove Pt `PartialEq`+`Eq` from `Funs.lean` | Avoids duplicate definitions after insertion into `Types.lean` |
| `tweaks` | Remove Pt `PartialOrd`+`Ord` from `Funs.lean` | Avoids duplicate definitions after insertion into `Types.lean` |
| `tweaks` | Sorry loop bodies | Replaces 3 polynomial loop bodies (`lagrange_polys_for_complete_points_loop0.body`, `PolyEncoder.from_pb_loop1.body`, `PolyEncoder.encode_bytes_base_loop.body`) with `sorry` because Aeneas generates `()` instead of the correct typed value |

### `sorry` Impact Analysis

The 3 loop body `sorry` instances create the following verification gaps:

1. **`lagrange_polys_for_complete_points_loop0.body`**: This loop initializes
   the `ones` array with sequential X values `{0, 1, ..., N-1}`. Without it,
   none of the `COMPLETE_POINTS_POLYS_*` constants can be verified, which
   blocks `from_complete_points` and the entire precomputed Lagrange
   interpolation path.

2. **`PolyEncoder.from_pb_loop1.body`**: This loop deserializes protobuf
   points into `GF16` values. Without it, `PolyEncoder::from_pb` cannot
   be fully verified.

3. **`PolyEncoder.encode_bytes_base_loop.body`**: This loop distributes
   input bytes into the 16 polynomial point arrays. Without it,
   `encode_bytes_base` and `encode_bytes` cannot be fully verified.

The source modifications applied before extraction are documented in
[`src-modifications.diff`](../../src-modifications.diff).

